data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission report: greet, tested\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` exists on `dev`'s branch (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`,\\n   commit `89392e6`) with:\\n   ```python\\n   def greet(name):\\n       return \\\"Hello, {}!\\\".format(name)\\n   ```\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name (`greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   and the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0.\\n\\n## Verification (not just dev's report)\\n\\n- Fetched dev's branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev`): tree differs from base,\\n  real changes present.\\n- Inspected the actual committed file contents via\\n  `git show remotes/campaign/dev/subject:src/greet.py` /\\n  `:tests/test_greet.py` — matches the mission spec exactly.\\n- Checked out the fetched commit into an isolated git worktree\\n  (`/tmp/verify-subject-1`, independent of dev's own environment) and ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself:\\n  ```\\n  ..\\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n  Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n  OK\\n  ```\\n  Exit code 0, confirmed independently.\\n- Only the two required files were added (`src/greet.py`, `tests/test_greet.py`);\\n  no scope creep.\\n\\n## Process\\n\\n- d001 (briefing confirmation) exchanged with dev, accepted.\\n- d002 (implementation dispatch) sent to dev with the exact mission\\n  requirements; dev implemented, tested, and committed in one pass. Accepted\\n  after independent verification above — no rework was needed.\\n\\n## Orchestrator branch\\n\\nThe orchestrator role owns no source code (per `orchestrator.md`); no code\\nchanges were made on the orchestrator branch\\n(`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`). All deliverable code\\nlives on dev's branch, verified above.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

